WEBVTT

00:08.800 --> 00:09.718
[electronic beep]

00:10.635 --> 00:11.553
[lower-pitched beep]

00:12.637 --> 00:13.638
[beeping continues]

00:13.722 --> 00:16.558
[warbling]

00:16.641 --> 00:18.268
[higher-pitched beeps]

00:19.894 --> 00:20.854
[high-pitched warbling]

00:20.937 --> 00:23.356
- [Asahi] Oh, it's working.
- [Momoka] What?

00:24.190 --> 00:25.859
Is that your phone, Asahi?

00:25.942 --> 00:28.445
- [crackling]
- [Asahi] No, it's the one I picked up.

00:31.114 --> 00:32.157
[Momoka] Is it recording?

00:32.240 --> 00:33.074
[Asahi] Yes.

00:34.492 --> 00:36.786
I'm pretty sure the camera's working.

00:58.391 --> 00:59.559
Unreal…

01:01.061 --> 01:02.395
There's no one in this town.

01:04.314 --> 01:07.317
Everyone in Tokyo
seems to have disappeared.

01:14.491 --> 01:16.284
We're in Harajuku and no one's here.

01:16.868 --> 01:17.994
[Asahi] Yeah.

01:27.879 --> 01:29.172
What's going on?

01:32.258 --> 01:33.843
[camera warbling, crackling]

01:36.805 --> 01:38.807
There's not a living soul around.

01:38.890 --> 01:40.350
It's been five days now.

01:41.726 --> 01:44.521
Taking another video?
What are you gonna do with them?

01:45.104 --> 01:46.105
Leaving a record.

01:46.815 --> 01:48.358
What's the point?

01:49.442 --> 01:51.152
Someone might see it one day.

01:54.155 --> 01:55.490
And after a little while,

01:56.783 --> 01:58.076
we met someone.

02:00.745 --> 02:01.871
There was this place…

02:02.872 --> 02:04.833
where we were taken to and…

02:06.751 --> 02:09.462
When we got there, we started working.

02:11.589 --> 02:12.799
[camera warbling]

02:16.803 --> 02:17.762
Okay?

02:18.346 --> 02:20.348
[ominous music]

02:28.940 --> 02:30.608
Are you seriously going in there?

02:32.318 --> 02:34.320
[ominous music builds]

02:45.039 --> 02:47.000
[echoing]
It's pitch black in here.

02:50.295 --> 02:51.254
Momoka?

02:52.297 --> 02:53.381
Momoka?

02:54.591 --> 02:55.717
Momoka!

02:55.800 --> 02:57.802
[ominous music crescendos]

03:06.561 --> 03:08.563
[theme music]

04:07.288 --> 04:09.290
[sinister music]

04:11.626 --> 04:13.628
[fire crackling]

04:16.547 --> 04:18.633
[fire roaring]

04:22.011 --> 04:24.722
[alarm beeping]

04:28.309 --> 04:29.227
[PA chiming]

04:29.310 --> 04:31.729
[announcer] Fifteen minutes remaining.

04:31.813 --> 04:33.815
[sinister music]

04:37.235 --> 04:39.237
[all panting, whimpering]

04:45.952 --> 04:47.203
Kill 'em all.

04:51.082 --> 04:53.084
[dire music]

04:53.167 --> 04:54.168
I…

04:55.003 --> 04:57.755
I can't do this anymore.
[sobs]

04:57.839 --> 04:58.965
We've got no choice.

04:59.048 --> 05:01.050
[sobbing]

05:02.969 --> 05:05.596
We'll never be the same again
after killing so many people.

05:06.764 --> 05:08.308
- [Jun yelps]
- [gun clatters]

05:08.933 --> 05:10.018
[Aguni] Did you hear me?

05:11.894 --> 05:14.272
Anyone who defies me here is the witch.

05:14.355 --> 05:15.273
[cocks gun]

05:15.356 --> 05:17.358
[tense music]

05:19.360 --> 05:20.528
Just shoot me then!

05:21.404 --> 05:22.488
[sobbing]

05:22.572 --> 05:23.531
[Arisu] That's enough!

05:30.121 --> 05:31.581
This ends now!

05:37.879 --> 05:38.796
You…

05:39.630 --> 05:41.466
You had me tied up the whole time.

05:41.549 --> 05:42.800
[breathes heavily]

05:42.884 --> 05:44.969
When the murder happened,
that's where I was.

05:46.095 --> 05:47.680
So that means that you know that…

05:48.723 --> 05:50.433
That I can't be the witch.

05:50.516 --> 05:52.185
[panting]

05:54.395 --> 05:57.940
And if you aren't the witch,
you don't need to kill me.

05:58.900 --> 06:02.028
Just work with me
and we'll find the witch!

06:12.663 --> 06:13.956
- [winces]
- [people clamor]

06:14.040 --> 06:15.208
- Arisu!
- [Aguni grunts]

06:16.000 --> 06:17.960
[Usagi whimpers]

06:18.044 --> 06:19.170
[Usagi] Stop it!

06:19.253 --> 06:20.963
[screams, whimpers]

06:21.047 --> 06:22.423
[Arisu grunts]

06:22.507 --> 06:23.841
[Usagi] I know everything!

06:23.925 --> 06:25.468
[panting]

06:25.551 --> 06:28.137
You're going after Arisu
even though you know he didn't do it.

06:29.430 --> 06:30.848
And that's…

06:30.932 --> 06:32.433
because you're the witch!

06:34.060 --> 06:36.020
- [grunts]
- Arisu!

06:36.104 --> 06:38.231
[breathing heavily]

06:43.569 --> 06:44.612
Are ya…

06:45.363 --> 06:46.364
the witch?

06:49.951 --> 06:52.161
[tense music]

06:54.497 --> 06:55.498
Yes.

06:56.415 --> 06:57.750
I am the witch.

06:57.834 --> 06:59.877
[people breathing nervously]

07:12.265 --> 07:13.099
[gun clatters]

07:18.896 --> 07:19.856
Go ahead.

07:22.650 --> 07:23.943
Do it!

07:26.028 --> 07:28.030
[tense music continues]

07:29.866 --> 07:31.200
Well, shoot him!

07:31.284 --> 07:32.618
[Arisu] Aguni is not the witch!

07:35.204 --> 07:37.373
It's a Ten of Hearts game!

07:37.457 --> 07:39.959
It plays with your feelings
and your emotions!

07:40.626 --> 07:42.879
You're not gonna win by killing Aguni.

07:42.962 --> 07:44.881
That's not the way this game works.

07:44.964 --> 07:46.966
[suspenseful music]

07:52.013 --> 07:53.431
I know you're not the witch.

07:54.599 --> 07:55.725
So why then?

07:57.143 --> 07:58.936
You gotta have another reason.

08:00.730 --> 08:02.064
What are you saying?

08:04.192 --> 08:05.651
The one that you killed

08:06.527 --> 08:07.695
wasn't Momoka.

08:09.530 --> 08:10.490
It was Hatter.

08:10.573 --> 08:11.991
[people murmuring]

08:12.074 --> 08:13.117
What?

08:19.457 --> 08:21.292
I could see it right away in your eyes.

08:22.752 --> 08:25.046
It was as if you lost all hope and…

08:26.422 --> 08:27.507
just gave up.

08:28.299 --> 08:29.592
I had the same feeling…

08:31.177 --> 08:32.970
when I killed my friends.

08:38.476 --> 08:39.852
You're not dumb.

08:40.645 --> 08:43.397
But as soon as you took over,
you wanted to kill everyone.

08:44.357 --> 08:45.733
And that's not like you.

08:47.360 --> 08:49.028
So you…
[grunts]

08:49.111 --> 08:50.947
…had to have another motive.

08:54.200 --> 08:55.952
Ever since I came to the Beach,

08:56.577 --> 08:58.120
I couldn't quite figure it out.

08:59.956 --> 09:01.958
If you had possession of all these guns,

09:02.667 --> 09:05.294
why didn't the militant corps take over
a long time ago?

09:06.212 --> 09:07.964
That never happened until now.

09:09.757 --> 09:10.841
Because in the end,

09:11.926 --> 09:14.303
you weren't against Hatter at all.

09:16.013 --> 09:17.890
Didn't you actually help each other out?

09:20.476 --> 09:22.478
You wanted to make sure that…

09:22.562 --> 09:25.106
scary people like Niragi
don't go ballistic.

09:26.732 --> 09:28.192
You tried to hold them back.

09:31.529 --> 09:33.531
[somber music]

09:37.702 --> 09:38.661
I know…

09:41.038 --> 09:42.790
how close you and Hatter were.
[groans]

09:42.873 --> 09:44.667
You were best friends, weren't you?

09:48.045 --> 09:49.589
Then, why did you kill him?

09:53.968 --> 09:55.219
I'll tell you why.

09:57.013 --> 10:00.099
Because you could never forgive him
for what he did.

10:02.727 --> 10:05.980
You wanted it all to stop,
but it was too late.

10:11.027 --> 10:13.738
You didn't recognize him anymore,
isn't that right?

10:18.200 --> 10:20.202
[melancholic music]

10:22.622 --> 10:24.624
[wind blowing]

10:25.583 --> 10:27.585
[footsteps]

10:41.057 --> 10:42.475
[Aguni] These crazy games…

10:44.352 --> 10:45.645
They're gonna continue?

10:50.858 --> 10:55.071
[Hatter] I will create a utopia here.
An oasis.

10:55.154 --> 10:57.365
[melancholic music builds]

10:57.448 --> 10:59.909
For all of those out there
who have lost hope…

11:02.286 --> 11:03.829
[inhales sharply]

11:03.913 --> 11:05.665
I offer the possibility

11:06.165 --> 11:07.833
of a better life!

11:11.295 --> 11:13.297
This will be where hope is born.

11:17.134 --> 11:18.260
That's impossible.

11:19.595 --> 11:20.554
Really?

11:20.638 --> 11:22.264
[inhales deeply]

11:22.348 --> 11:23.182
[loud pat]

11:24.308 --> 11:25.976
We can do it together.

11:30.356 --> 11:32.316
[crowd cheering]

11:33.651 --> 11:35.444
Hear my words now.

11:36.362 --> 11:37.988
We're all in this together.

11:39.281 --> 11:42.451
We're going to unite
and gather all the cards…

11:43.077 --> 11:45.037
and get back to the world we knew!

11:45.121 --> 11:47.415
[crowd cheering]

11:48.374 --> 11:50.376
[melancholic music]

11:52.420 --> 11:54.380
[Hatter breathing heavily]

11:55.798 --> 11:56.674
[sniffles]

11:57.591 --> 11:58.676
[Hatter] Idiots…

11:59.677 --> 12:02.471
thought they could hide
their playing cards from me.

12:05.015 --> 12:07.351
[man 1 whimpering, choking]

12:11.147 --> 12:14.400
- [Hatter grunting]
- [loud pounding]

12:17.611 --> 12:19.613
[Hatter panting]

12:24.910 --> 12:25.953
Aguni.

12:28.789 --> 12:29.790
[Hatter sniffles]

12:30.875 --> 12:32.585
As of this day,

12:35.337 --> 12:38.007
there will be a new rule.

12:40.801 --> 12:41.719
[Hatter sniffles]

12:46.807 --> 12:49.185
"Death to any traitor."

12:56.150 --> 12:57.860
You don't know anything!

13:03.616 --> 13:04.533
- [smash]
- [Arisu grunts]

13:04.617 --> 13:06.368
[screams]

13:06.452 --> 13:07.495
[Usagi] Stop it!

13:07.578 --> 13:10.039
[Arisu groaning]

13:10.122 --> 13:11.457
[Tatta grunts]

13:11.540 --> 13:12.917
[Usagi yells]

13:13.000 --> 13:13.918
[Arisu groans]

13:15.836 --> 13:17.296
- [gags]
- [Aguni snarls]

13:17.379 --> 13:19.381
[breathing heavily]

13:23.636 --> 13:24.762
You know nothing.

13:26.931 --> 13:27.932
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

13:28.015 --> 13:29.642
[car engine rumbles]

13:34.104 --> 13:35.064
[engine turns off]

13:37.733 --> 13:38.651
[car door shuts]

13:38.734 --> 13:39.735
[man 2] This way.

13:49.954 --> 13:51.539
[melodic chiming on PA]

13:51.622 --> 13:53.249
[announcer] Congratulations.

13:56.252 --> 14:00.214
[Hatter whistling]

14:04.677 --> 14:05.719
[whistling stops]

14:05.803 --> 14:07.972
[ominous music]

14:08.055 --> 14:10.224
[Hatter] That brings back memories.

14:12.059 --> 14:14.436
This place really hasn't changed at all.

14:19.900 --> 14:20.901
[Aguni] Look…

14:23.112 --> 14:24.280
I'm done.

14:27.074 --> 14:29.910
We're losing control of Niragi
and the militant corps.

14:33.914 --> 14:35.583
Let's get rid of the Beach.

14:40.254 --> 14:41.297
[Hatter] Get rid of it?

14:43.716 --> 14:45.843
Every member of the Beach

14:46.510 --> 14:50.055
is consumed with the happiness
that they found there.

14:50.890 --> 14:53.017
Getting back to the old world
by gathering a few cards

14:53.100 --> 14:54.935
was just a lie you came up with.

14:59.315 --> 15:00.399
We need to end this.

15:03.068 --> 15:04.069
So you're…

15:04.904 --> 15:06.447
betraying me, then?

15:13.287 --> 15:15.873
"Death to any traitor," right?

15:18.167 --> 15:20.878
That's the rule of the Beach,
remember that.

15:20.961 --> 15:22.463
The Beach means nothing!

15:23.255 --> 15:24.465
Just stop this.

15:27.259 --> 15:30.930
I wanted to instill hope,
to create a utopia!

15:31.013 --> 15:33.515
It's bullshit, and you know it!
[breathing heavily]

15:34.475 --> 15:36.310
There is no hope here.

15:40.147 --> 15:41.398
This world we're in…

15:43.025 --> 15:44.818
has crushed all hope.

15:55.287 --> 15:56.246
You see,

15:59.166 --> 16:01.418
I used to have friends with me
I could trust.

16:04.463 --> 16:05.881
But all the hope I had…

16:09.093 --> 16:10.427
died along with them.

16:14.932 --> 16:16.225
[shudders]

16:27.403 --> 16:28.862
Sometimes, a king…

16:31.782 --> 16:34.076
is in a position where he has
to make decisions

16:34.159 --> 16:35.577
that are painfully hard.

16:41.166 --> 16:42.668
Like right now,

16:44.253 --> 16:45.337
my friend.

16:49.508 --> 16:51.093
[cocks gun]

17:04.273 --> 17:05.274
[gunshot]

17:05.357 --> 17:07.359
[somber music]

17:09.278 --> 17:11.613
I know what it feels like
to see your friends die.

17:13.157 --> 17:15.951
To kill them, I see it.

17:17.286 --> 17:19.997
You killed your friend.
I see it in your eyes.

17:21.415 --> 17:24.376
And now you just wanna kill everyone here,

17:24.460 --> 17:27.671
because they were the ones
who made your friend crazy.

17:30.632 --> 17:34.887
These painful feelings of yours,
the game master is using all of them.

17:36.638 --> 17:39.600
That's why it's a game of Hearts.
Don't you get that?

17:39.683 --> 17:41.894
- Shut up!
- [Arisu grunts]

17:41.977 --> 17:42.811
Arisu!

17:44.104 --> 17:46.523
So if all of this is true, then…

17:46.607 --> 17:49.818
Aguni wanted to kill everyone
no matter what the game was.

17:51.945 --> 17:53.530
He had you do it.

17:54.281 --> 17:56.825
And we said nothing
and went along with it all.

17:59.078 --> 18:03.207
So, who here is the witch then?

18:04.458 --> 18:05.709
[Arisu] I know who it is.

18:07.711 --> 18:09.171
I know who the real witch is.

18:12.758 --> 18:14.301
[Arisu breathes shakily]

18:14.885 --> 18:16.887
A game master…

18:16.970 --> 18:19.431
uses similar characteristics
in every game.

18:22.059 --> 18:23.393
In a game of Hearts,

18:24.436 --> 18:27.314
he usually makes a fool out of everyone.

18:28.816 --> 18:31.568
[announcer] Difficulty, Seven of Hearts.

18:31.652 --> 18:34.363
A game of betrayal plays with our hearts.

18:34.446 --> 18:35.364
It's bullshit!

18:35.447 --> 18:36.323
[device warbles]

18:36.406 --> 18:37.699
[monitor boings, cheering]

18:38.700 --> 18:40.869
It looks like the wolf
is the one that needs to hide!

18:42.496 --> 18:44.123
It might be that…
[shudders]

18:45.916 --> 18:48.001
…there really was a way to end the game…

18:49.962 --> 18:51.922
without having to kill everyone.

18:54.049 --> 18:55.300
A solution where…

18:56.802 --> 18:58.595
nobody has to get hurt,

18:59.513 --> 19:00.848
and no one has to die.

19:02.724 --> 19:05.394
But… that's impossible.

19:06.562 --> 19:08.564
We have to hunt down the witch

19:08.647 --> 19:10.607
and burn them
in the Fire of Judgment, right?

19:11.775 --> 19:13.318
[inhales sharply]
No.

19:18.991 --> 19:20.325
[Arisu panting]

19:22.119 --> 19:24.037
The witch could be right here and…

19:25.414 --> 19:26.790
no one dies.

19:26.874 --> 19:28.876
[somber music]

19:31.295 --> 19:32.421
Because it's…

19:34.173 --> 19:36.717
Momoka. She was the witch all along.

19:38.844 --> 19:41.221
[crowd murmuring]

19:51.565 --> 19:54.735
So, wait.
She stabbed herself in the chest?

19:55.861 --> 19:57.070
[Arisu] Yes.

19:58.572 --> 20:01.700
If I were the game master…
[sniffles]

20:01.783 --> 20:03.577
…that's what I would come up with.

20:03.660 --> 20:05.662
[somber music]

20:07.998 --> 20:09.374
- [groans]
- [thuds]

20:10.000 --> 20:12.669
You're full of shit!
[panting]

20:12.753 --> 20:14.171
I'm the witch!

20:15.380 --> 20:18.300
You all wanna kill me, right?

20:22.471 --> 20:23.680
[growls]

20:23.764 --> 20:25.599
[crowd screaming]

20:26.683 --> 20:27.726
[grunts]

20:29.269 --> 20:31.855
Aguni's trying
to take everyone down with him.

20:32.648 --> 20:34.691
- [crowd screaming]
- [Aguni grumbles]

20:34.775 --> 20:35.984
[man 3 groans]

20:36.985 --> 20:38.487
[grunts]

20:38.570 --> 20:39.529
[shrieks]

20:40.072 --> 20:41.823
[men growling]

20:41.907 --> 20:43.909
- [Aguni hisses]
- [crowd clamoring]

20:46.745 --> 20:48.705
[choking]

20:48.789 --> 20:50.707
[breathing heavily]

20:57.130 --> 20:59.132
[somber music]

21:14.815 --> 21:15.816
[cocks gun]

21:20.612 --> 21:23.198
[sobbing]

21:26.535 --> 21:28.036
Oh, Takeru.

21:30.330 --> 21:32.416
[sobbing]

21:32.499 --> 21:33.458
Hey.

21:34.084 --> 21:36.878
Takeru. Takeru.

21:39.339 --> 21:40.424
Takeru!

21:41.758 --> 21:42.676
[sobs]

21:44.845 --> 21:47.389
[wails]

21:48.765 --> 21:50.976
This Beach made him crazy.

21:51.059 --> 21:52.311
Do you hear me?

21:52.394 --> 21:54.688
- [grunting]
- You guys made him crazy!

21:54.771 --> 21:56.315
[grunts]

21:58.108 --> 22:00.152
Kill me, I'm the witch!

22:00.235 --> 22:01.361
[grunts]

22:05.324 --> 22:08.160
Listen.
I know how to stop Aguni, trust me!

22:10.162 --> 22:11.663
I'll get his attention, all right?

22:12.247 --> 22:13.999
Burn Momoka in the Fire of Judgment.

22:16.001 --> 22:16.835
Arisu.

22:18.879 --> 22:21.048
This whole thing has to stop now, okay?

22:21.548 --> 22:23.550
[clamoring continues]

22:26.261 --> 22:27.512
Asahi!

22:27.596 --> 22:28.805
[grunting]

22:30.682 --> 22:31.683
[Asahi] Everyone!

22:34.644 --> 22:36.104
I'm the one!

22:36.188 --> 22:38.440
The dealer of this game!

22:39.232 --> 22:40.734
[mechanical whirring]

22:40.817 --> 22:41.985
[laser zaps]

22:50.452 --> 22:51.495
[thuds]

22:54.122 --> 22:56.083
[silence]

23:06.676 --> 23:08.678
[panting]

23:09.971 --> 23:11.431
[Ann] It was a reverse grip.

23:16.812 --> 23:20.774
Fingerprints with a reverse grip
were found on the knife.

23:20.857 --> 23:22.651
[panting]

23:27.656 --> 23:30.117
[Momoka trembling]

23:30.200 --> 23:31.201
[Ann] That means

23:32.410 --> 23:34.663
that Momoka grabbed
the handle of the knife

23:35.413 --> 23:37.290
and stabbed it through her own chest.

23:38.291 --> 23:42.504
- [breathing heavily]
- [grunts]

23:45.715 --> 23:47.175
She was the witch.

23:47.259 --> 23:49.261
[somber music]

23:52.222 --> 23:53.849
But why would she do that?

23:54.891 --> 23:56.560
It couldn't have been just for the game.

23:57.519 --> 24:00.730
So Momoka was really…
the game master after all?

24:02.524 --> 24:04.276
And that girl said she was the dealer.

24:06.987 --> 24:09.948
So they were just toying with us
the whole time, then?

24:12.868 --> 24:15.537
So there was never any high power
doing all this?

24:16.413 --> 24:17.455
They were just human?

24:21.459 --> 24:22.711
But it's possible that…

24:24.337 --> 24:26.923
they could've been
controlled by somebody else.

24:33.763 --> 24:34.806
[Arisu] Aguni.

24:36.433 --> 24:38.393
[breathing heavily]

24:38.476 --> 24:39.728
We need to stop this.

24:41.271 --> 24:43.273
No more innocent people have to die.

24:44.649 --> 24:46.109
Too many people have already.

24:47.861 --> 24:50.113
[somber music continues]

24:50.197 --> 24:54.409
I understand how it feels…
to kill your friends.

24:55.744 --> 24:57.287
But we can't take it out on…

24:58.288 --> 25:00.582
people who are still alive!

25:03.293 --> 25:04.920
We are still alive!

25:06.254 --> 25:08.215
We're all in this together…

25:09.549 --> 25:12.093
and we have to fight to end it all!

25:13.178 --> 25:15.347
[somber music]

25:15.931 --> 25:18.850
I don't want anybody else to die!

25:23.355 --> 25:25.357
[panting]

25:48.421 --> 25:50.423
[fire crackling]

25:51.049 --> 25:52.300
The fire is spreading!

25:53.510 --> 25:55.262
- [crowd clamoring]
- Run!

25:58.390 --> 26:00.976
- Hurry! Put her in the Fire of Judgment!
- Hurry, run!

26:02.686 --> 26:03.687
- [gunshots]
- [groans]

26:04.562 --> 26:05.814
- [gunshots]
- [groans]

26:05.897 --> 26:07.649
- [gunshots]
- [shrieking]

26:08.692 --> 26:11.111
[Niragi breathing heavily]

26:12.320 --> 26:13.154
[Niragi] That hurt.

26:14.781 --> 26:17.242
[crowd murmuring]

26:19.828 --> 26:22.163
If I could do it all over again,

26:22.247 --> 26:24.040
[breathing heavily]

26:24.833 --> 26:28.420
I'd use this Fire of Judgment
to burn this whole place down!

26:29.129 --> 26:31.298
- [man 4] Niragi…
- [woman 1] Niragi?

26:33.091 --> 26:35.969
And that will make me the winner!

26:36.928 --> 26:39.347
[people screaming]

26:39.431 --> 26:40.307
[gunshots]

26:49.107 --> 26:51.651
[whimpering, yelps]

26:52.235 --> 26:53.236
[grunts]

26:54.321 --> 26:55.655
[gunshots]

27:01.286 --> 27:03.496
[tense music]

27:03.580 --> 27:06.041
- [clamoring, screaming continues]
- [gunshots]

27:06.124 --> 27:07.500
[shrieks]

27:07.584 --> 27:09.336
[grunting]

27:09.419 --> 27:10.295
Get off me!

27:10.378 --> 27:12.047
- [Usagi grumbles]
- [Arisu grunts]

27:12.130 --> 27:13.715
- [Usagi whimpers]
- [pounding]

27:13.798 --> 27:15.717
[Niragi] I'm gonna kill you!

27:17.135 --> 27:18.386
- [yells]
- [Usagi screams]

27:18.470 --> 27:19.804
[Arisu grunts]

27:20.722 --> 27:22.849
[grumbles, panting]

27:22.932 --> 27:24.351
[Usagi whimpers]

27:25.477 --> 27:26.853
[panting]

27:31.691 --> 27:33.526
You are dead.

27:33.610 --> 27:36.071
I'll kill you all!

27:37.822 --> 27:39.240
- [clicks]
- [gunshot]

27:41.534 --> 27:42.452
[grunts]

27:43.328 --> 27:44.621
- [gunshots]
- [groans]

27:46.081 --> 27:48.583
[screaming]

27:48.666 --> 27:49.834
[Niragi winces]

27:49.918 --> 27:51.878
[screaming fades out]

27:53.463 --> 27:54.631
[gunshots]

27:54.714 --> 27:56.716
[somber chorale music]

27:58.343 --> 27:59.636
Aguni.

27:59.719 --> 28:02.889
[panting, gasps]

28:02.972 --> 28:04.974
[somber chorale music continues]

28:08.478 --> 28:09.479
[PA chimes]

28:09.562 --> 28:12.232
[announcer] Three minutes
remaining in the game.

28:12.315 --> 28:13.525
We need to hurry!

28:13.608 --> 28:15.151
[pants]

28:17.654 --> 28:18.613
[Ann] Grab her legs.

28:18.696 --> 28:20.281
- [clamoring]
- [Ann] Ready? Now lift!

28:21.658 --> 28:23.660
[clamoring]

28:26.996 --> 28:28.206
[man 5] Come on!

28:29.416 --> 28:31.418
Hurry! Move, move, move!

28:31.501 --> 28:33.795
[panting]

28:37.882 --> 28:40.135
[breathing heavily]

29:04.451 --> 29:06.453
[somber chorale music builds]

29:18.757 --> 29:20.216
[phone chiming melodically]

29:23.511 --> 29:24.971
[announcer] Congratulations.

29:25.054 --> 29:26.973
GAME CLEARED
CONGRATULATIONS

29:29.434 --> 29:31.436
[somber chorale music]

29:34.397 --> 29:37.817
[Last Boss] There is no safe place
for us in this world.

29:43.364 --> 29:46.910
When the first explorers
discovered the north pole,

29:46.993 --> 29:48.953
the world was unspoiled

29:49.037 --> 29:51.998
and spared of the burden of civilization.

29:54.083 --> 29:58.880
And when it is all said and done,
we simply return to the soil.

30:01.758 --> 30:02.926
This land

30:03.551 --> 30:05.678
is a mirror to the world.

30:07.388 --> 30:09.557
I am thankful to this place.

30:09.641 --> 30:11.726
[fire crackling]

30:12.519 --> 30:13.436
For now…

30:15.104 --> 30:18.316
I'm freer than ever before.

30:27.951 --> 30:29.953
[somber chorale music builds]

30:44.467 --> 30:46.553
This is the end of our paradise.

30:47.679 --> 30:49.722
[fire crackling]

30:54.727 --> 30:56.604
So many of us died.

30:58.773 --> 30:59.774
[sobs]

31:11.327 --> 31:13.329
[cries]

31:17.292 --> 31:18.418
I don't think I…

31:19.460 --> 31:20.753
can ever forgive them.

31:23.006 --> 31:25.383
- Let me go!
- You can't.

31:26.759 --> 31:28.553
[cries]

31:28.636 --> 31:29.762
But they…

31:30.847 --> 31:32.432
They killed 'em all!

31:33.182 --> 31:34.475
I can't let that go!

31:34.559 --> 31:36.519
[Tatta crying]

31:42.025 --> 31:43.401
[inhales deeply]

31:43.484 --> 31:44.319
[clicks]

31:44.402 --> 31:46.362
[sobbing]

31:51.618 --> 31:53.661
[breathing heavily]

31:58.458 --> 31:59.542
Let's stop this.

32:01.544 --> 32:04.213
Everyone here, we're still alive.

32:06.257 --> 32:08.301
And that's all that matters right now.

32:10.803 --> 32:12.096
That's all that matters.

32:12.180 --> 32:13.139
[thuds]

32:13.222 --> 32:14.182
Arisu?

32:15.224 --> 32:16.059
Arisu!

32:17.185 --> 32:19.187
[emotional music]

32:23.858 --> 32:25.818
[sobs]

32:34.035 --> 32:35.244
I get it now.

32:38.665 --> 32:39.499
[sobs]

32:41.250 --> 32:42.627
I understand.

32:43.503 --> 32:44.545
Arisu…

32:48.257 --> 32:50.259
[emotional music]

33:05.441 --> 33:07.276
[fire crackling]

33:31.300 --> 33:33.011
You never quit, do you?

33:38.016 --> 33:41.352
I was starting to think
collecting these cards was pointless.

33:41.436 --> 33:42.979
[chuckles]
What do you think now?

33:44.397 --> 33:45.690
I'm thinking that…

33:47.066 --> 33:49.736
we still haven't seen
any of the face cards.

33:49.819 --> 33:51.821
[sinister music]

33:52.447 --> 33:57.076
And so what is it
the game's controllers want us to see?

34:07.837 --> 34:09.756
- [Momoka] Is it recording?
- [Asahi] Yes.

34:11.090 --> 34:13.718
I'm pretty sure the camera's working.

34:17.972 --> 34:19.265
[Usagi] What is this?

34:20.141 --> 34:22.101
It's a video that Asahi left behind.

34:25.063 --> 34:26.147
[Asahi] Unreal…

34:27.940 --> 34:29.400
There's no one in this town.

34:31.027 --> 34:33.988
Everyone in Tokyo
seems to have disappeared.

34:35.740 --> 34:36.741
[camera whirs]

34:36.824 --> 34:38.117
And after a little while,

34:39.202 --> 34:40.912
we met someone.

34:43.122 --> 34:44.290
There was this place…

34:45.291 --> 34:47.085
where we were taken to and…

34:49.212 --> 34:51.756
When we got there, we started working.

34:56.052 --> 34:57.428
We helped with…

34:58.471 --> 35:00.598
preparing and executing the games.

35:03.976 --> 35:05.520
Are you seriously going in there?

35:15.196 --> 35:17.281
[Asahi] There are people known as dealers

35:18.032 --> 35:20.076
who help facilitate the games.

35:22.245 --> 35:23.329
[echoing stomp]

35:24.038 --> 35:29.085
Sometimes we actually join the games
or act as taggers.

35:30.461 --> 35:32.964
Everyone thinks
we are just regular players,

35:33.881 --> 35:36.092
and part of our job is to confuse them.

35:37.760 --> 35:38.678
But…

35:39.262 --> 35:42.682
during the games,
we're being watched the entire time,

35:43.641 --> 35:47.395
and we'll be killed if anyone
ever finds out that we're the dealers.

35:48.980 --> 35:52.817
Are you recording again?
What are you gonna do if they find out?

35:54.527 --> 35:55.778
[camera flicks off, on]

35:58.030 --> 36:00.032
[footsteps echoing]

36:08.040 --> 36:11.043
[keypad beeping]

36:11.127 --> 36:12.044
[door unlocks]

36:12.128 --> 36:15.381
BEWARE OF ELECTROCUTION
TRAIN CABLES ABOVE

36:15.464 --> 36:17.091
[door creaks softly]

36:24.807 --> 36:26.601
Is this where the game master is?

36:27.476 --> 36:29.478
[footsteps]

36:29.562 --> 36:31.564
[eerie music]

36:40.573 --> 36:42.575
[eerie music crescendos]

36:54.253 --> 36:56.255
[eerie music]

37:03.721 --> 37:05.723
[eerie music builds]

37:13.689 --> 37:15.441
[distorted indistinct chatter]

37:15.524 --> 37:16.859
[man 6] Stop!

37:16.943 --> 37:18.653
[woman 2 screams]

37:18.736 --> 37:20.529
They're really going at it!

37:20.613 --> 37:22.490
[indistinct chatter]

37:36.462 --> 37:38.130
- All right, yes, yes!
- [laughs]

37:38.214 --> 37:40.091
[indistinct shouting]

37:42.593 --> 37:45.012
[woman 3 screaming]

37:45.096 --> 37:47.265
DEALER WINS

37:48.182 --> 37:50.184
[laughter]

37:53.354 --> 37:54.438
Who are they?

37:56.899 --> 37:59.402
So these are all the game masters?

38:02.530 --> 38:03.656
[camera flicks on]

38:08.911 --> 38:09.870
[sighs]

38:10.496 --> 38:12.123
So many have died.

38:13.416 --> 38:16.585
[sobs]
I remember one girl around our age.

38:19.338 --> 38:21.132
Our job was…
[sobs]

38:21.716 --> 38:23.884
…to make sure the game went
the way they wanted it,

38:24.468 --> 38:27.179
and we joined in.
[sighs]

38:27.263 --> 38:29.473
And we made sure many players died.

38:30.766 --> 38:32.059
Because of us,

38:33.894 --> 38:35.855
many people die every day.

38:37.356 --> 38:39.358
[Momoka sobbing on video]

38:40.276 --> 38:41.861
[Momoka] I can't take this anymore.

38:45.364 --> 38:47.616
We kill people, win the game,

38:48.409 --> 38:49.869
and earn visa days.

38:54.999 --> 38:57.460
[sobs]
We get to live for another two weeks,

38:57.543 --> 38:59.920
but I don't even know
how many people I've…

39:01.797 --> 39:04.050
[sobs]
I can't do it anymore.

39:05.634 --> 39:07.428
Momoka.
[sobs]

39:08.929 --> 39:11.474
This is all a dream.

39:14.310 --> 39:16.103
- It's all right.
- [whimpers]

39:17.104 --> 39:19.148
We're going to wake up
from this nightmare soon.

39:19.231 --> 39:21.150
[weeping]

39:25.446 --> 39:27.448
[Momoka sobbing]

39:32.328 --> 39:34.580
[Momoka] I want it all to be over…

39:34.663 --> 39:36.624
[both weeping]

40:04.985 --> 40:06.153
[Arisu] So this is it.

40:17.039 --> 40:17.998
[echoing stomp]

40:19.083 --> 40:20.000
[thuds]

40:32.179 --> 40:34.140
[footsteps]

40:43.691 --> 40:44.817
There it is.

40:51.365 --> 40:56.871
BEWARE OF ELECTROCUTION
TRAIN CABLES ABOVE

41:03.002 --> 41:04.378
[door clunks, squeaks]

41:35.242 --> 41:37.244
[eerie music]

41:57.389 --> 41:59.391
[eerie music continues]

42:38.055 --> 42:40.057
[eerie music builds]

42:54.488 --> 42:56.532
[eerie music continues]

43:00.744 --> 43:02.204
I don't believe it.

43:12.464 --> 43:14.758
[Chishiya] So you actually
found this place.

43:21.015 --> 43:23.309
I expected no less from you.

43:26.854 --> 43:28.147
[Kuina] Long time no see.

43:31.025 --> 43:32.109
What's going on?

43:34.486 --> 43:38.282
Thanks to you two, I have
all the numbered playing cards right here.

43:39.241 --> 43:40.200
Thank you.

43:42.369 --> 43:44.038
How did you find this place?

43:47.041 --> 43:50.044
It took me a while,
but I figured out that this is actually

43:50.127 --> 43:52.046
the map of a subway station.

43:53.464 --> 43:56.008
[eerie music]

44:08.437 --> 44:10.731
So what happens
when we collect all the cards?

44:11.649 --> 44:15.486
I thought coming here
would provide me with an answer.

44:16.612 --> 44:19.698
But I gotta tell you,
I only know one thing.

44:20.491 --> 44:22.826
These people aren't the game masters,
are they?

44:24.286 --> 44:25.329
Right.

44:26.413 --> 44:27.706
What's pretty clear is

44:28.374 --> 44:30.834
they were all killed after our victory.

44:31.502 --> 44:34.797
They're just humans like us,
and the kicker is…

44:36.298 --> 44:37.591
there's someone above them.

44:45.432 --> 44:47.893
So, then… who could they be?

44:49.353 --> 44:50.354
Who knows?

44:51.689 --> 44:52.856
Maybe aliens.

44:55.401 --> 44:56.693
Maybe God.

44:59.238 --> 45:01.031
[lights zooming]

45:05.411 --> 45:08.122
SPECIAL URGENT BROADCAST

45:08.205 --> 45:10.207
[fanfare music playing]

45:12.000 --> 45:15.421
[Mira] Congratulations to all players.

45:19.133 --> 45:20.259
Huh?

45:21.802 --> 45:22.719
Oh.

45:24.304 --> 45:26.306
[sinister music]

45:27.057 --> 45:28.225
[Arisu] Mira.

45:29.351 --> 45:30.436
[electronic warbling]

45:30.519 --> 45:32.438
Except for the face cards,

45:32.980 --> 45:35.441
you've all completed the numbered games

45:36.024 --> 45:37.860
and emerged victorious.

45:38.902 --> 45:41.572
And the prize of these sweet victories

45:41.655 --> 45:44.533
was the sacrifice of many lives.

45:47.077 --> 45:47.911
[soft warbling]

45:49.121 --> 45:50.164
I wonder…

45:51.457 --> 45:54.460
just how many
of your close friends have died?

45:55.002 --> 45:57.004
[sinister music]

45:59.423 --> 46:01.008
Do you remember…

46:01.633 --> 46:03.635
[static]

46:03.719 --> 46:05.512
…the ones who were shot in the head?

46:05.596 --> 46:07.723
[screaming, clamoring on videos]

46:08.891 --> 46:10.726
That girl you burned alive…

46:10.809 --> 46:12.728
[indistinct yelling]

46:15.230 --> 46:17.024
The ones struck down by lasers…

46:17.107 --> 46:18.609
[people screaming]

46:18.692 --> 46:20.319
Or the ones who drowned?

46:20.402 --> 46:22.362
[clamoring]

46:23.113 --> 46:24.823
[man 7] Help me!

46:24.907 --> 46:26.950
The ones whose heads were blown off?

46:27.659 --> 46:29.203
Your friends.

46:30.370 --> 46:32.080
- [monitors warbling]
- [people screaming]

46:32.164 --> 46:34.291
All that despair you felt…

46:34.374 --> 46:35.542
- [Arisu] Karube!
- [explosion]

46:35.626 --> 46:39.213
[Mira] Those gruesome scenes,
you'll never forget them.

46:39.296 --> 46:41.548
[people screaming on videos]

46:42.466 --> 46:43.634
And that…
[sobs]

46:44.384 --> 46:45.969
…really touches me.

46:46.553 --> 46:49.264
[Mira sobbing]

46:51.183 --> 46:52.100
[warbling]

46:52.184 --> 46:54.102
To all surviving players,

46:55.103 --> 46:56.230
we just wanted

46:57.523 --> 46:59.149
to give you a present.

47:00.692 --> 47:02.778
Going back to our world?

47:02.861 --> 47:04.029
[exclaims]

47:05.781 --> 47:07.366
There will be new games!

47:07.449 --> 47:09.451
[tense music]

47:10.244 --> 47:13.914
Let's all play,
and this time with all the face cards!

47:15.457 --> 47:16.750
New games?

47:18.043 --> 47:19.628
I don't hate that idea.

47:20.337 --> 47:21.588
[Mira laughs]

47:21.672 --> 47:26.009
We've got so many more wonderful
and exciting games in store for you all,

47:26.760 --> 47:28.053
so be prepared.

47:30.681 --> 47:31.974
[Usagi] So then…

47:32.808 --> 47:34.309
Is she the game master?

47:36.144 --> 47:38.272
I think I'd rather see an alien up there.

47:39.565 --> 47:42.568
The next stage starts tomorrow,

47:43.569 --> 47:45.404
when the clock strikes noon.

47:45.487 --> 47:46.572
[static]

47:46.655 --> 47:48.198
Let's have some fun,

47:48.991 --> 47:50.450
all together!

47:52.119 --> 47:53.954
So we have to fight once again.

47:55.330 --> 47:56.248
Yeah.

47:58.458 --> 47:59.835
But there's one difference.

47:59.918 --> 48:02.129
[suspenseful music]

48:03.380 --> 48:05.841
Now we know what our target looks like.

48:09.511 --> 48:12.306
[fireworks blasting]

48:23.108 --> 48:24.026
[wind blows]

48:24.109 --> 48:26.111
[ominous music]

48:28.447 --> 48:30.699
[papers rustling]

48:36.955 --> 48:38.957
[grandiose music]

48:46.840 --> 48:49.509
SHIBUYA CENTER STREET

48:49.593 --> 48:51.261
[airship engine rumbling]

48:51.345 --> 48:53.263
SHIBUYA STATION

49:05.484 --> 49:07.486
[engine rumbling louder]

49:33.512 --> 49:35.555
That's where we'll find our answers.

49:37.432 --> 49:39.434
[bold rock music]

49:41.353 --> 49:43.355
[airship engine whooshes]
